{"availability":"available","full":"srirangaraj-b/UNOQ_STM32_HAL","name":"UNOQ_STM32_HAL","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"C++","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-15T11:06:03Z","updated":"2026-10-03T08:45:44Z","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":null,"color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z","discoveredVia":[],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A high-performance, register-level Hardware Abstraction Layer (HAL) library designed specifically for the STM32U585 microcontroller on the Arduino UNO Q.","This library bridges the gap between the Zephyr-based Arduino core and direct hardware control, offering robust, low-overhead support for GPIO, PWM Generation, PWM Input Capture, and ADC Analog Readings—fully optimized for rigid hardware layouts."],"features":["Advanced GPIO Control: Fast atomic bit-manipulation (BSRR), direct register access, and automatic alternate-function (AF) release to force system-locked pins into pure software GPIO mode.","Hardware PWM Output: Multi-channel support across STM32 timers (TIM1, TIM2, TIM3, TIM4, TIM5, TIM8, TIM15, TIM16, TIM17) with preloaded duty cycles, frequency scaling, dead-time insertion, and complementary outputs.","PWM Input Capture: Hardware-assisted frequency and duty cycle measurement using timer input capture modes.","Flexible ADC Helpers: 12-bit analog input reading supporting both string-based pin names (e.g., \"PA0\") and native GPPin objects, with built-in millivolt conversion and safe Zephyr ADC initialization.","Arduino Compatibility: Seamless integration with standard Arduino APIs and libraries (such as LiquidCrystal)."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/srirangaraj-b/UNOQ_STM32_HAL/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"9145a57ced0ff5e2dab00e8de40cca437f4e32365919a35e5891aebbecdd7cea","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A high-performance, register-level Hardware Abstraction Layer (HAL) library designed specifically for the STM32U585 microcontroller on the Arduino UNO Q.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/srirangaraj-b/UNOQ_STM32_HAL/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"9145a57ced0ff5e2dab00e8de40cca437f4e32365919a35e5891aebbecdd7cea","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/srirangaraj-b/UNOQ_STM32_HAL/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-03T08:45:44Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/srirangaraj-b/UNOQ_STM32_HAL/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z","hash":"9145a57ced0ff5e2dab00e8de40cca437f4e32365919a35e5891aebbecdd7cea","originalBytes":3936,"storedBytes":3936,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["pin","stm","arduino","adc","pwm","int","pa0","cpp","duty","hardware","lcd.print","tim3","analog","gpio","input","libraries","library","liquidcrystal","raw","serial.print","setup","using","void","analogread","analogreadmillivolts","capture","delay","e.g.","false","frequency","hal","include","lcd.setcursor","millivolts","objects","output","read","reading","sensorpin","stm32","uno","bit","change","control","core","cycle","direct","example","khz","lcd","loop","name","pinmode","rawval","robust","serial.println","standard","stm32u585","support","unoq","usage","value","via","voltage","abstraction","access","across","active","advanced","af2","alternate-function","api","apis","atomic","automatic","available","between","bit-manipulation","board","both","bridges","bsrr","built-in","calculated","channel","clone","columns","compatibility","complementary","const","convenience","conversion","converted","cycles","dead-time